pmdomain: core: Fix two problems removing a genpd

Both show up when a PSCI domain probe defers and removes its domains again,
which happens on every boot of a Moto G Power (2021) with SM6115 and an MPM
power domain as the system domain's parent. That part of its device tree is
in another series, so plain v7.4-rc1 doesn't reproduce these there.

The first is a lockdep report, and only wrong on PREEMPT_RT. The second is
memory corruption on any kernel: fw_devlink's links can outlive the genpd
holding the device they point at, which has been possible since commit
3b7b8acacf37 and shows up with SLUB debugging.

There's one more report in the same area that this doesn't fix. Lockdep
also reports "Invalid wait context" for MPM's domain, which uses a regular
spinlock and goes through mbox_send_message() in its power_off, under the
raw locks of the CPU domains. That is also only wrong on PREEMPT_RT. Since
that report turns lockdep off, these were tested with a local patch that
marks MPM's domain as a CPU domain and overrides the wait type around the
mailbox call, neither of which is meant to go upstream.

Tested with lockdep, SLUB debugging and kmemleak on, and after that with
those off. Not tested on PREEMPT_RT, and on no other SoC.
